Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Yonghui,

1) I would export the raw data from Fleximaging if possible. Only if the file is too large to work with, I would recommend binning during data export.
2) As I said I guess the resolution function does strange things when applied to a centroided file. In case you expect more features it could be that you have to decrease SNR during peak picking. To me 2700 features sounds pretty high, are you sure you are expecting so many peaks?
3) mzAlign can be used with known m/z for recalibration, but what I mean is that it can also align m/z shifts between spectra to the medium spectrum and I absolutely needed it for all low resultion data I analyzed.

Best,
Melanie

